  "heading_path": [
    "Trade Marks Act 1995",
    "Part 13—Importation of goods infringing Australian trade marks",
    "136  Claim for release of seized goods"
  ],
  "instrument": "TMA1995",
  "kind": "section",
  "number": "136",
  "ref": "TMA1995/s136",
  "text": "(1) The designated owner may make a claim to the Comptroller-General of Customs for the release of seized goods. Note: For designated owner and seized goods see section 6. (2) The claim must be made before the end of the claim period for the goods. Note: For claim period see section 6. (3) The claim must contain the information prescribed by the regulations. Note: Sections 137.1 and 137.2 of the Criminal Code create offences for providing false or misleading information or documents.",
  "title": "Claim for release of seized goods",
